# --- SecBrain frontend: how the browser finds the API ---
#
# The API base URL is resolved AT RUNTIME in the browser, so the app works when
# opened from another device/host without rebuilding. Pick one of:
#
# 1) Leave BOTH unset (recommended for LAN / self-hosting):
#    The browser derives the API from the page's own host and NEXT_PUBLIC_API_PORT.
#    Open http://<server-ip-or-host>:3000 and the API targets
#    http://<server-ip-or-host>:8000 automatically.
#    Requires: backend reachable on that host:port, and SECBRAIN_CORS_ALLOW_ALL=true
#    (or add the exact origin to SECBRAIN_CORS_ORIGINS) on the backend.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_API_PORT=8000
#
# 2) A fixed public API URL (e.g. a domain or public IP):
# NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL=https://api.your-domain.example
#
# 3) Same-origin (best for a reverse proxy / tunnel that serves UI + API on one
#    URL): the browser uses relative /api paths. Put a proxy in front that routes
#    /api/* to the backend (see docs/TROUBLESHOOTING.md). No CORS needed.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL=same-origin
